---
import DemoLayout from '../../components/DemoLayout.astro'
---

<DemoLayout
  title="Measure"
  description="A measure lab for Hairline: the new 78ch / 22px reading default against the previous 68ch / 19px, full-bleed and the 78ch / 19px anti-example."
  current="/demos/measure/"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-reading">
      <p class="font-ui text-label-11 uppercase text-ink-tertiary">Measure lab</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-ui text-heading-32 font-semibold text-ink">A measure, four ways.</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[54ch] font-prose text-copy-18 text-ink-secondary">
        The new reading default is 78ch at 22px. Compare it with the previous
        68ch / 19px, a full-bleed object, and the same 78ch at 19px.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-3">
        <div class="z-segmented max-sm:flex-wrap" role="group" aria-label="Measure treatment">
          <button type="button" class="z-segmented__item" data-measure-option="new" aria-pressed="true">New default</button>
          <button type="button" class="z-segmented__item" data-measure-option="before" aria-pressed="false">Before</button>
          <button type="button" class="z-segmented__item" data-measure-option="bleed" aria-pressed="false">Full-bleed</button>
          <button type="button" class="z-segmented__item" data-measure-option="wide" aria-pressed="false">78ch / 19</button>
        </div>
        <p class="font-ui text-label-12 text-ink-tertiary" data-measure-note>
          78ch · 22px · about 81 characters. The new reading default.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="measure-article mt-16" data-measure-article data-measure="new">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="measure-column mx-auto max-w-reading">
        <header class="mb-8 border-b border-line pb-6">
          <h2 class="mt-0 font-prose text-heading-40 font-semibold text-ink max-sm:text-heading-32">The Quiet Page</h2>
          <p class="measure-deck mt-4 max-w-[56ch] font-prose text-lede-24 text-ink-secondary max-sm:text-copy-18">What a reading interface owes the reader.</p>
          <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-2 font-ui text-label-12 tabular-nums text-ink-tertiary">
            <time datetime="2026-10-22">2026.10.22</time>
            <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
            <span>12 min</span>
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="z-prose z-prose--numbered" lang="en">
          <p class="z-lede">
            A page is a promise: nothing here is more interesting than the
            sentence you are reading. Most interfaces break that promise before
            the first paragraph. The ones that keep it are not simpler. They are
            more deliberate.
          </p>

          <h2 id="the-measure">The measure</h2>
          <p>
            Reading happens in a line, and a line has a length. Too short and
            the eye bounces from one ragged edge to the other; too long and it
            loses its place on the return. The typographic answer is old and
            unglamorous: set a measure, then defend it.
          </p>
          <p>
            A measure is a range in characters, not a width in pixels. The
            typeface, the size and the reader's settings all change it. The new
            reading measure is 78ch at 22px: about 81 characters. The old 68ch
            at 19px was about 80. The same 78ch at 19px would be about 94; the
            larger body is what makes the wider column work.
          </p>

          <figure class="measure-bleed measure-quote">
            <blockquote>Typography exists to honor content.</blockquote>
            <figcaption>Robert Bringhurst</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <h2 id="the-numbers">The numbers</h2>
          <p>
            The classic range is 45–75 characters. Most web reading lands
            between 60 and 70; 80 is the upper bound, not a target. The new
            default is at 81, the old one at 80: both sit at the top of the
            range. The wider column and the larger body were chosen together.
          </p>

          <div class="measure-bleed measure-table">
            <table class="z-table">
              <caption class="sr-only">A comparison of the four treatments.</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Treatment</th>
                  <th>Body</th>
                  <th>Column</th>
                  <th class="text-right tabular-nums">Characters</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>New default</td><td>22px / 1.68</td><td>78ch</td><td class="text-right tabular-nums">≈ 81</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Before</td><td>19px / 1.68</td><td>68ch</td><td class="text-right tabular-nums">≈ 80</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Full-bleed</td><td>22px / 1.68</td><td>78ch</td><td class="text-right tabular-nums">≈ 81</td></tr>
                <tr><td>78ch / 19</td><td>19px / 1.68</td><td>78ch</td><td class="text-right tabular-nums">≈ 94</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p>
            Widening the text column alone makes every number worse. The new
            default widens the column and raises the body; the full-bleed option
            keeps the measure and lets the object use the shell; 78ch at 19px
            is the anti-example.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="shell mt-24 border-t border-line pt-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-reading">
      <p class="font-ui text-label-11 uppercase text-ink-tertiary">The range</p>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div>
          <p class="font-prose text-heading-24 text-ink">45–75</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-ui text-label-12 text-ink-tertiary">Bringhurst's classic range</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-prose text-heading-24 text-ink">60–70</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-ui text-label-12 text-ink-tertiary">The practical web target</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-prose text-heading-24 text-ink">≤ 80</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-ui text-label-12 text-ink-tertiary">The upper bound, not a goal</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-[58ch] font-prose text-copy-16 text-ink-secondary">
        The best measure is a property of the face and the size, not of the
        screen. A 1440px monitor does not ask for a 1440px line; it asks for a
        reading column and a good use of the space around it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</DemoLayout>

<script>
  const article = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-measure-article]')
  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-measure-option]')
  const note = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-measure-note]')

  const notes: Record<string, string> = {
    new: '78ch · 22px · about 81 characters. The new reading default.',
    before: '68ch · 19px · about 80 characters. The previous measure.',
    bleed: '78ch · 22px; the quote and table use the shell. The text measure does not move.',
    wide: '78ch · 19px · about 94 characters. The anti-example.',
  }

  const set = (value: string) => {
    if (!article) return
    article.dataset.measure = value
    for (const button of buttons) {
      button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button.dataset.measureOption === value))
    }
    if (note) note.textContent = notes[value] ?? ''
  }

  for (const button of buttons) {
    button.addEventListener('click', () => set(button.dataset.measureOption ?? 'new'))
  }
</script>

<style>
  .measure-article[data-measure='before'] .measure-column {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .measure-article[data-measure='before'] .z-prose {
    font-size: 19px;
  }

  .measure-article[data-measure='before'] .z-prose .z-lede {
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .measure-article[data-measure='before'] .measure-deck {
    font-size: 20px;
  }

  .measure-article[data-measure='wide'] .z-prose {
    font-size: 19px;
  }

  .measure-article[data-measure='wide'] .z-prose .z-lede {
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .measure-article[data-measure='wide'] .measure-deck {
    font-size: 20px;
  }

  .measure-article[data-measure='bleed'] .measure-bleed {
    width: min(var(--z-layout-shell), calc(100vw - 2 * var(--z-layout-gutter)));
    margin-left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }

  .measure-quote {
    margin-block: 2.5em;
  }

  .measure-quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    color: var(--z-color-ink);
    font-family: var(--z-font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .measure-quote figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--z-space-4);
    color: var(--z-color-ink-tertiary);
    font-family: var(--z-font-ui);
    font-size: var(--z-text-label-11);
    line-height: var(--z-leading-label-11);
    letter-spacing: var(--z-tracking-label-11);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .measure-article[data-measure='bleed'] .measure-quote blockquote {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .measure-table {
    margin-block: 2.5em;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .measure-table table {
    display: table;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 34rem;
    margin-block: 0;
  }
</style>
